WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.209
Music Playing

00:00:01.209 --> 00:00:02.252
Dear diary,

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:04.546
Today I start you, my video diary,

00:00:05.046 --> 00:00:08.607
because well in a nutshell,

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.176
everything in my life is changing.

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:18.309
I’m Bonnie Hunt, writer, director and executive producer of the new Apple TV Plus series, Amber Brown.

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:19.060
Oh yeah.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:19.811
Very cool!

00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:23.322
I’m Sarah Drew and I play Amber’s mom.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:25.692
Who just so happens to also be called Sarah.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:30.989
Amber is a girl who is just starting middle school and going through a lot of changes.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:34.451
So she uses her video diary and sketching to kind of help her through that.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.662
I love that you're doing your art, but you know, you also need people,

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:39.998
Friends are good to have.

00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:42.709
Hi! I’m Brandi with an ‘I’.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:46.296
I like to think about it as kind of like the yin and yang symbol.

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:51.051
Amber is very introverted and Brandi is an extrovert.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:55.305
Sometimes I think I like to be one of them for a day, but then I'd miss myself.

00:00:55.847 --> 00:00:59.476
They're so different, but they really balance each other out.

00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:00.727
You're unusual.

00:01:01.144 --> 00:01:01.686
Thank you.

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:03.063
Now that’s a compliment.

00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:11.696
The show is inspired by the books entitled Amber Brown, written by Paula Danziger, and woven into the childhood of many girls and boys.

00:01:11.696 --> 00:01:17.077
My best friend Justin is moving to Alabama. And my mom’s got a boyfriend. It’s weird.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:25.418
We walk through every single thing that this sweet little girl is going through by getting a window into her life, through video diaries.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.253
And through her sketches,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.257
Earlier today, I walked smack into a pillar right in front of the cutest boy in the whole school.

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:32.008
Oh!

00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:35.303
Some of those come to life in full animation.

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:42.435
It’s kind of a way for the audience to not only hear what Amber says in front of everybody, but to see what she’s feeling in her deepest inner thoughts.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:43.436
I'm cool.

00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:47.982
What I saw in the script, the characters were really beautifully developed.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:49.150
It was funny.

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:57.200
It was innovative in the way that we get inside of the mind of this eleven year old who’s going through huge changes in her life.

00:01:57.325 --> 00:01:59.369
Do you wanna sit together? For lunch?

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:01.412
Yeah.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:07.252
The show is from Amber's point of view, but it really is about all families and a lot of kids at this age,

00:02:07.252 --> 00:02:12.215
you know, that pre teenage years, life can feel overwhelming at times and complicated.

00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:13.049
There's my girl!

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:18.429
We get a window into the beauty of how family can take lots of different shapes.

00:02:20.765 --> 00:02:21.641
This is so exciting.

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:31.568
You could be going through the most intense problem ever, and you could just crack up right in the middle of it. 

00:02:31.776 --> 00:02:36.489
All the things that Amber goes through real people go through which can really help you feel like you’re not alone.

00:02:36.614 --> 00:02:38.533
This is the best day ever!

00:02:38.575 --> 00:02:39.576
I’ll never forget this.

00:02:39.576 --> 00:02:42.720
♪♪

